# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Node.js app (Express 5, TypeScript, EJS, Knex) sold in tiers: {{TIERS_LABEL}}. Core
({{CORE_TIER_LABEL}}) lives in `src/` and `views/`; each higher tier is a module in `modules/<tier>/`.
A client release contains only the tiers that client has, because `scripts/build-release.sh`
removes the rest from the code.

## Getting started

```bash
npm install
npm run migrate
npm run create-user -- admin admin
npm run dev
```

## Tiers

- `{{PREFIX_UPPER}}_TIER` in `.env` picks the active tier. Development defaults to `{{TOP_TIER}}`.
- `npm run feature` lists feature switches; `npm run feature -- <name> --on` (or `--off`,
  `--reset`) changes one.
- In views: `<% if (can("perm")) { %>…<% } %>`, `can(["a", "b"], { any: true })`, `featureOn("name")`,
  and `<%- include("partials/menu", { section: "main" }) %>`. On routes: `requirePermission("perm")`.
- A module exports `register(context)` (routes, switches, permissions, menu items) and its
  `migrations`. Core never imports from `modules/`; `test/arch.test.ts` enforces it.

Run the suite at every tier before committing:

```bash
for tier in {{TIERS_SPACED}}; do {{PREFIX_UPPER}}_TIER=$tier npm test || break; done
```

## Releases

```bash
scripts/build-release.sh <tier> <version>    # e.g. scripts/build-release.sh {{CORE_TIER}} 1.0.0
```

The script writes a fresh one-commit repo and a zip to `../<project>-releases/` and prints the
SHA-256. The zip contains compiled `dist/` and production `node_modules/`: on the server run
`node dist/src/cli/migrate.js`, then `npm start`. Paths that never ship are listed in `release.exclude`.

## AI agents

`AGENTS.md` has the rules for coding agents, including the commit review gate. A human approves
every commit; `scripts/propose-commit.sh` asks for that approval on the terminal.
